    cours: {"lede":"Quatorze grands crus, de Marlenheim au nord à Kintzheim au sud, souvent plus petits que ceux du Haut-Rhin.","frise":null,"essentiel":"Le Bas-Rhin compte 14 des 51 grands crus, environ 353 ha selon le CIVA ; le plus grand est le Frankstein (56,20 ha), le plus petit le Kastelberg (5,82 ha).","sections":[{"h":"Les 14 crus et leur surface","blocs":[{"imp":"utile","txt":"Surfaces données par le CIVA ; le cahier des charges ne cite que celle de l’Engelberg (14,80 ha), identique."}],"table":{"caption":"Les grands crus du Bas-Rhin et leur surface (CIVA)","head":["Grand cru","Commune(s)","Surface"],"rows":[{"imp":"utile","cells":["Altenberg de Bergbieten","Bergbieten","29,07 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Altenberg de Wolxheim","Wolxheim","31,20 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Bruderthal","Molsheim","18,40 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Engelberg","Dahlenheim et Scharrachbergheim-Irmstett","14,80 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Frankstein","Dambach-la-Ville","56,20 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Kastelberg","Andlau","5,82 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Kirchberg de Barr","Barr","40,63 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Moenchberg","Andlau et Eichhoffen","11,83 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Muenchberg","Nothalten","17,70 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Praelatenberg","Kintzheim","18,70 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Steinklotz","Marlenheim","40,60 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Wiebelsberg","Andlau","12,52 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Winzenberg","Blienschwiller","19,20 ha"]},{"imp":"utile","cells":["Zotzenberg","Mittelbergheim","36,45 ha"]}]}}],"synthese":[{"imp":"essentiel","txt":"14 grands crus dans le Bas-Rhin, environ 353 ha."},{"imp":"important","txt":"Frankstein le plus grand (56,20 ha), Kastelberg le plus petit (5,82 ha)."}],"src":"CIVA (Vins d’Alsace), brochure « Grands crus d’Alsace » (Brochure_D13_Grands_Crus, vinsalsace.com ; version anglaise lue), p. 12, tableau des surfaces, consultée le 30 oct. 2026 ; BO-agri, cahier des charges des 51 AOC Alsace grand cru (15 janv. 2026) ; fiche 865 du site."},
